 "_doc": "Casing drops, bullet impacts and flybys, all sliced from the real Sonniss recordings (no synthesis). casings.<kind>.<material>: list of source specs. {drops:{long,short}} = auto-slice a long take into its individual fresh drops (long = drop + bounce / roll tail up to 1.6 s, short = first 0.28 s); {single:true} = the file is one drop. pitch = semitones applied to the slice (shell proxies from small casings are pitched down); proxy:true marks material that is not a real recording of that exact thing (see docs/AUDIO.md coverage). variants = extra per-source takes (pitch / eq / gain) for single-file sources. A kind never cuts one drop twice (casing_takes): with few drops in a take a key gets fewer, distinct variants; rifle metal (proxy) takes the 9 mm drops rifle concrete leaves. Carpet takes are low-passed at 6 kHz (a few drops ping off another casing; a casing on carpet is dull). Casings ship mono (point_source).",
